---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="bononokoko" description="Personal site — portfolio, writing, and small experiments in one place.">
  <a href="/making" class="eyebrow project-back">← making</a>
  <h1>bononokoko</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    The site you're browsing — a personal home on the web for projects, essays, photos, and a
    few quiet experiments. Built and redesigned by me, room by room.
  </p>

  <div class="project-actions">
    <a class="cta" href="/">Explore the live site →</a>
    <a href="https://github.com/keeeeeliu/website" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Source code →</a>
  </div>

  <p class="project-meta">Personal project · keeeeliu.io · 2025–2026</p>

  <section>
    <h2>Why I Built It</h2>
    <p>
      I wanted one place that felt like mine — not a LinkedIn export or a generic portfolio
      template. Somewhere to show work with context, publish writing in both English and Chinese,
      and leave room for things that don't fit a résumé: bunny photos, a listening corner, collected
      quotes. The structure came from that intent: a house with rooms, not a list of tabs.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="project-grid">
    <div>
      <h2>What It Is</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/making">making</a> — projects and the process behind them</li>
        <li><a href="/words">words</a> — essays and short fragments</li>
        <li><a href="/moments">moments</a> — an informal photo log</li>
        <li><a href="/sounds">sounds</a> — a small listening room with ambient tracks</li>
        <li><a href="/bunnies">the bunnies</a> — a living diary for Chris &amp; Oliver</li>
        <li><a href="/collected">collected</a> — excerpts and things worth keeping</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>What I Built</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Room-based navigation with a sticky header and page-to-page transitions.</li>
        <li>A custom earthy-retro design system — typography, palette, responsive card grid.</li>
        <li>Content collections for essays, fragments, quotes, moments, and bunny diary entries.</li>
        <li>A persistent background-music dock with an audio-reactive vinyl visualizer.</li>
        <li>Reveal-on-scroll animations with reduced-motion fallbacks.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Stack</h2>
    <p>
      Astro, MDX content collections, TypeScript, view transitions (<code>ClientRouter</code>),
      vanilla CSS with design tokens, Web Audio API for the music visualizer, deployed to
      GitHub Pages at <a href="https://keeeeliu.io" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">keeeeliu.io</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>A Note</h2>
    <p>
      This project page lives inside the thing it describes — which is either recursive or honest,
      depending on your tolerance for meta. Either way, the craft is in the details: how a room card
      feels on hover, where the bunny hops, whether the music visualizer respects
      <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code>. That's the kind of frontend work I care about.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .project-back {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .project-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 1.6rem 0 1rem;
  }

  .project-actions a:not(.cta) {
    color: var(--terracotta);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .project-meta {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  section {
    margin: 2.2rem 0;
  }

  .project-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(220px, 0.8fr);
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  li {
    margin: 0.45rem 0;
  }

  section ul a {
    color: var(--terracotta);
  }

  section code {
    font-size: 0.88em;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--border) 55%, transparent);
    padding: 0.12rem 0.35rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .project-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
